<title>USA: Carter to attend food conference in Ethiopia.</title>
<headline>Carter to attend food conference in Ethiopia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former U.S. President Jimmy Carter will attend a workshop in Ethiopia to discuss investments aimed at boosting farm output in sub-Saharan Africa, the Carter Center in Atlanta said Monday.</p>
<p>After the Aug. 23-27 workshop, Carter and his wife will travel to Mali and Mozambique in support of his center's &quot;global development initiative.&quot;</p>
<p>The initiative, set up in 1993, works with governments and international donor agencies to support economic and social development in emerging democracies.</p>
</text>
